title: "entropy-lens: Token-level entropy trajectories from LLM logprobs"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Lim"
    given-names: "Leo"
    email: "dlatmdals99@gmail.com"
repository-code: "https://github.com/leo-im/entropy-lens"
url: "https://github.com/leo-im/entropy-lens"
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-08-08"
keywords:
  - llm
  - entropy
  - uncertainty
  - logprobs
  - interpretability
abstract: >-
  A lightweight Python library that computes and visualizes token-level
  entropy trajectories from LLM logprobs. Works from single-pass logprobs
  only — no multi-sampling or auxiliary models — making it suitable for
  serving pipelines and information-theoretic reliability research.
